---
// Privacy note. Every statement here must stay true: re-check it when hosting, analytics, embeds or mail change.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHead from '../components/PageHead.astro';
import { email } from '../lib/site';
---

<Base title="Privacy" description="What this site does, and does not do, with your data.">
  <PageHead title="Privacy" lead="Short version: this site sets no cookies, runs no analytics and tracks nobody." />

  <section class="sec">
    <p class="label mono">01 — Who</p>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>I, Stefano Zaghi, run this site. For anything about your data, write to me at <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec">
    <p class="label mono">02 — This site</p>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>No cookies, no analytics, no tracking, no advertising, no third-party embeds. Fonts, images and videos are served
        from this site itself, so visiting it sends no request to anyone else.</p>
      <p>If you use the light/dark switch, your browser remembers the choice in its local storage (key <code>theme</code>).
        It stays on your device and is never sent anywhere; clearing your browser data removes it.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec">
    <p class="label mono">03 — Hosting</p>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>The site is a set of static files hosted by GitHub Pages (GitHub, Inc.). Like any web server, GitHub receives your
        IP address with each request and may log it for security and operations, under the
        <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub privacy statement</a>.
        The domain's DNS is managed by Cloudflare; page requests do not pass through Cloudflare.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec">
    <p class="label mono">04 — Email</p>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>Mail sent to {email} is forwarded by Cloudflare Email Routing to my personal inbox
        (<a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare privacy policy</a>). I use it only to reply to you,
        never share it, and delete it on request.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec">
    <p class="label mono">05 — Your rights</p>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>Under the GDPR you can ask what data about you is held, and have it corrected or deleted: write to the address
        above. Links to other sites (GitHub, ORCID, doi.org, the code documentation) lead to services with their own
        policies.</p>
      <p class="mono updated">Last updated 13 November 2026.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .updated { color: var(--text-3); }
</style>
